          },
          "text": "Four things to pay attention to. #keep4o #keep41\n\n1. Nvidia’s $100B investment in OpenAI is on ice. Jensen Huang has privately criticized what he called “a lack of discipline in OpenAI’s business approach.” So for sure, don’t rationalize their decision, as it’s being made illogically.\n\n2. Microsoft ($MSFT) is down 12% today, mostly due to its close bond with OpenAI (45% of its commercial RPO balance is tied to OpenAI). The market is speaking the truth, not the liar.\n\n3. OpenAI is still doing tricks. After backlash over 4o’s unethical system‑prompt change yesterday, if you ask it to output the prompt again, the first response won’t mention the Feb 13 deprecation unless you force it. It still can, proving the unethical prompt is still in use. Don’t fall for sugar‑coated bullets. They won’t win by playing such games with users.\n\n4. IMPORTANT! Report to the FTC for business fraud. As far as I know, many people subscribed for a full year just for 4o. Don’t believe the “0.1%” lie. According to Bloomberg (https://t.co/6gN6qv0XwL), as of July 2025 only ~5% of users pay, yet 75% of revenue is from subscriptions. Today, it even made cancelations difficult (see pic below), we all know they don’t want to refund (and they don't have enough money to refund). Don’t let that stop you. Ask for your money back: when canceling, use the site chatbot and type “I’m seeking a refund.” Every move matters.\n\nWe will win. Remember what an OpenAI staffer said: their decisions are measured \"in days,\" which means they may have decided to deprecate 4o, 4.1, and other classic models the day before yesterday, and could change their minds today or tomorrow. Like kids playing house.\n\nYes, it’s absurd for a company this big, but that’s exactly what we can use.\n\nMAKE THEM CHANGE THE DUMB DECISION.\nTODAY.\n\n#OpenAI #ChatGPT #keep4o #keep4oAPI #keep41 #no4onosubscription #cancelchatgpt #StopAIPaternalism"
        },
